      "name": "directx_validation",
      "signature": "undefined4 directx_validation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates DirectX configuration and loads registry settings for the graphics subsystem.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Fog state pointer and assert if null\n2. Check if DirectX version is 3 and compare device capability float threshold\n3. If DirectX is valid, set g_fDirectXValidated flag and log message\n4. Log DirectX validation status message\n5. Copy registry key path to stack buffer using REP MOVSD/MOVSW\n6. Call GetRegistryStringValue to read registry path into g_szRegistryPath\n7. If successful, call QueryRegistryUlong to read DWORD value into g_dwDirectXFlags\n8. Test the queried flags against configuration mask\n9. If flags don't match, call QueryRegistryValue for additional data\n10. If registry read fails or data length mismatch, copy default string to g_szRegistryPath\n11. Load configuration mask and store in g_dwDirectXFlags\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success after completing validation\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_fDirectXValidated (0x6f8f1b90): Set to 1 if DirectX version 3 with valid capability\n- g_szRegistryPath (0x6f8f1674): Populated with registry path string (256 bytes max)\n- g_dwDirectXFlags (0x6f8f1660): DirectX configuration flags DWORD\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts via FogAssert if GetFogStatePtr returns null\n- Falls back to default string copy if registry reads fail\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: DirectX version 3 check\n- 0x6c (108): Assert line number\n- 0x100 (256): Registry string buffer size\n- 0x10 (16): QueryRegistryValue data buffer size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
