      "name": "InitializeDirectDrawWindowEx",
      "signature": "dword InitializeDirectDrawWindowEx(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the DirectDraw windowed mode display surface and resolution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if DirectDraw window is already initialized (g_fDirectDrawWindowInitialized)\n2. If already initialized, return 0 (early exit)\n3. Call CloseDirectDrawWindow to ensure clean state\n4. Assert that primary surface does not already exist\n5. Load video configuration from global pointer\n6. Set default resolution to 640x480 (0x280 x 0x1E0)\n7. Determine bit depth based on video capabilities:\n   - 0x20 (32-bit) if high color flag set\n   - 0x18 (24-bit) if alternate color flag set  \n   - 0x10 (16-bit) default\n8. Log resolution and bit depth via QueueLogMessage\n9. Call IDirectDraw::SetDisplayMode via vtable offset 0x54\n10. If SetDisplayMode fails, log error via LogDirectDrawError and return 0\n11. Initialize DDSURFACEDESC structure (zero 0x1A dwords via STOSD.REP)\n12. Set structure size (0x6C), flags (DDSD_CAPS), and caps (DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE | DDSCAPS_FLIP)\n13. Call IDirectDraw::CreateSurface via vtable offset 0x18\n14. If CreateSurface fails, log error and return 0\n15. Set initialization flags and return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 on successful initialization, 0 on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x280 = 640 pixels (default width)\n0x1E0 = 480 pixels (default height)\n0x10 = 16-bit color depth\n0x18 = 24-bit color depth\n0x20 = 32-bit color depth\n0x6C = sizeof(DDSURFACEDESC)\n0x54 = IDirectDraw::SetDisplayMode vtable offset\n0x18 = IDirectDraw::CreateSurface vtable offset\n0x4200 = DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE | DDSCAPS_FLIP",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:b51da30e22e3d80dfbb6bee602f86d68",
