      "name": "ConvertPaletteToSurface",
      "signature": "int ConvertPaletteToSurface(byte * pDestBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Locks DirectDraw surface and converts indexed palette data to RGB format\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate 0x70 (112) bytes on stack for DDSURFACEDESC2 and buffer pointer array\n  2. Initialize array of 26 (0x1a) surface buffer pointers to NULL\n  3. Return 0 if DirectDraw surface descriptor is not initialized (g_ddSurfaceDesc == NULL)\n  4. Lock surface using method at offset 0x64 (100) in surface descriptor\n  5. Return 0 if lock operation fails\n  6. Iterate through screen width (outer loop)\n  7. For each column, iterate through screen height (inner loop)\n  8. Read palette index from surface row buffer\n  9. Convert palette index to RGB triplet using palette table entries\n  10. Write 3 bytes (RGB) to destination buffer per pixel\n  11. Unlock surface using method at offset 0x80 (128) in surface descriptor\n  12. Return 1 on success, 0 if unlock operation fails\n\nParameters:\n  pDestBuffer (ECX) - Pointer to destination buffer that receives RGB pixel data\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success: surface was locked, palette converted to RGB, and surface unlocked\n  0 - Failure: surface not initialized, lock failed, or unlock failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Early return if g_ddSurfaceDesc is NULL (no DirectDraw surface available)\n  Error logging via FUN_6f8e2450 if lock operation fails (error message at s_Lock_failed__6f8ed894)\n  Error logging via FUN_6f8e2450 if unlock operation fails (error message at s_Unlock_failed__6f8ed8a4)\n  Surface row pointer obtained from apbStack_68[3] for pixel data access",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
