      "name": "SetPaletteData",
      "signature": "void SetPaletteData(dword * pPaletteSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies 288 bytes (72 DWORDs) of palette color data from source buffer to the global palette buffer and updates the global palette data pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI and EDI registers for MOVSD operation\n2. Set loop counter to 0x48 (72 DWORDs = 288 bytes)\n3. Copy 72 DWORDs from pPaletteSource to g_aPaletteBuffer using REP MOVSD\n4. Update g_pPaletteData to point to g_aPaletteBuffer (0x6f885218)\n5. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pPaletteSource (ECX) - Pointer to source palette data buffer containing 288 bytes (72 DWORD RGBX color entries)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n  Side Effect: Updates g_aPaletteBuffer with copied palette data\n  Side Effect: Sets g_pPaletteData to point to g_aPaletteBuffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x48 (72) - Number of DWORDs to copy (72 * 4 = 288 bytes palette data)\n  0x6f885218 - Address of g_aPaletteBuffer global buffer\n  0x6f885210 - Address of g_pPaletteData global pointer\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n  pdVar2/iVar1 - Phantom SSA variables representing EDI/ECX registers during REP MOVSD loop; no actual storage, cannot be renamed via API",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
