      "name": "InitializeDirectDrawDisplay",
      "signature": "dword InitializeDirectDrawDisplay(dword dwReserved, dword dwDisplayMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initialize or reinitialize the DirectDraw display surface based on release mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current DirectDraw release mode flag from global memory (g_dwDirectDrawReleaseMode)\n2. If release mode is active (non-zero):\n   - Return success code (1) without reinitializing display\n3. If release mode is inactive (zero):\n   - Close current DirectDraw window via CloseDirectDrawWindow()\n   - Initialize new DirectDraw window via InitializeDirectDrawWindow(dwDisplayMode)\n   - Return result code from initialization function\n4. Function assumes display device is in valid state before call\n\nParameters:\n- dwReserved (dword): Reserved parameter, unused (passed via ECX in __fastcall)\n- dwDisplayMode (dword): Display mode/configuration flags to pass to InitializeDirectDrawWindow()\n\nReturns:\n- dword: Success code (1) if already in release mode, or initialization result code from InitializeDirectDrawWindow()\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwDirectDrawReleaseMode is non-zero, function short-circuits and returns immediately\n- Used during DirectDraw initialization sequences and display mode switches\n- Does not preserve existing display state when reinitializing\n\nMemory/Globals:\n- Reads: g_dwDirectDrawReleaseMode (dword at 0x6f8f1bcc)\n- Side effects: Modifies DirectDraw display device state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
