      "name": "RenderFormattedText",
      "signature": "void RenderFormattedText(dword nXPos, dword nYPos, LPCSTR szFormat, dword argList)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders formatted text to screen surface using 8x16 character bitmaps.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Format string using wvsprintfA with variable arguments into 512-byte buffer\n  2. Initialize X,Y starting coordinates and character index counter\n  3. Process each character in formatted string:\n     a. Check if X coordinate is within screen bounds (< 0x281 pixels)\n     b. For characters < 0x20 (control chars): skip rendering, use zero width\n     c. For printable chars (0x20-0x7F): render 8x16 bitmap to screen surface\n     d. For newline (0x0A): advance Y by 0x0C pixels, reset X to starting position\n  4. Character rendering inner loop:\n     a. Calculate screen destination from Y*stride + surface base + X\n     b. Lookup bitmap offset from g_aCharBitmapOffsets table\n     c. Copy 16 rows x 8 pixels from bitmap to surface (set pixel to 0xFF if non-zero)\n     d. Advance X by character width from g_aCharWidths table\n\nParameters:\n  nXPos (ECX): Starting X pixel coordinate (0 to 0x280 / 640)\n  nYPos (EDX): Starting Y pixel coordinate\n  szFormat (Stack+4): Format string for wvsprintfA (printf-style format)\n  argList (Stack+8): Variable argument list for format string substitution\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Characters beyond 0x280 pixels are clipped (not rendered, width=0)\n  - Negative X values use direct offset lookup for partial character rendering\n  - Newlines wrap to next line (Y + 0x0C, X reset to nXPos)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x280 (640) - Maximum X coordinate (screen width boundary)\n  0x0C (12) - Line height in pixels for newline advancement\n  0x10 (16) - Bitmap height in rows per character\n  0x08 (8) - Bitmap width in columns per character\n  0x20 (32) - ASCII space, first printable character\n  0xFF - Foreground pixel value when rendering\n\nGlobals:\n  g_dwScreenHeight (0x6f8f1784) - Screen row stride in pixels\n  g_dwRenderSurfaceLocked (0x6f8f177c) - Locked surface pixel buffer pointer\n  g_aCharWidths (0x6f8f1bd8) - Character width lookup table (96 entries)\n  g_aCharBitmapOffsets (0x6f8f1d58) - Character bitmap offset table (96 entries)\n  g_pCharBitmapData (0x6f8f1edc) - Character bitmap data base address",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:422c2f132c2b2af576dfa7c61e5f3ba056574217942d3e4352c9325c94df3404",
