      "name": "ClearRenderSurface",
      "signature": "void ClearRenderSurface(int nUseOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clear the DirectDraw render surface with optional width adjustment\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize local surface capability structure (0x64 = DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE)\n  2. Check if g_pRenderSurface exists (address 0x6f8f1bb4)\n  3. Call surface Lock method (vtable offset 0x14) with parameters:\n     - x=0, y=0, rect=NULL, flags=0x400 (DDLOCK_WAIT)\n     - Output: surface capability structure containing locked surface info\n  4. Check return value and compare with error code 0x887601ae (DDERR_SURFACELOST)\n  5. If DDERR_SURFACELOST:\n     - If nUseOffset != 0: Clear (width - 0x2f) * height bytes\n     - Otherwise: Clear full width * height bytes\n     - Use STOSD for DWORD-aligned clearing, STOSB for remainder\n  6. If other error: Call LogDirectDrawError with error code\n  7. Return with render surface locked (no unlock call)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX nUseOffset - If non-zero, adjust clear width by -0x2f (47 decimal)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Surface remains locked after function returns\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called only when DDERR_SURFACELOST occurs\n  - Uses g_dwScreenWidth (address 0x6f8f1b8c)\n  - Uses g_dwScreenHeight (address 0x6f8f1784)\n  - Destination: g_dwRenderSurfaceLocked (address 0x6f8f177c)\n  - Error logging via LogDirectDrawError with string at 0x6f8ee304",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:10c12fba63e5a70d7dcade551588d469",
