      "name": "GetTransformModeAndPalette",
      "signature": "int GetTransformModeAndPalette(int nPaletteIndex, dword * pdwPaletteResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves transform mode and palette lookup result for a given palette index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reads a dword from g_awData_6f899466 lookup table at [index*4] offset\n2. Stores that value in the output parameter pdwPaletteResult\n3. Uses a jump table to return the transform mode based on nPaletteIndex:\n   - Index 0: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x8 (transform mode 2)\n   - Index 1: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x4 (transform mode 2)\n   - Index 2: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x0 (transform mode 2)\n   - Index 3: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x104 (transform mode 1)\n   - Index 4: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x108 (transform mode 1)\n   - Index 5: Returns 0 (invalid - falls through to default)\n   - Index 6: Returns value from g_pOutputBufferTable+0x10c (transform mode 1)\n   - Index >6: Returns 0 (invalid index)\n\nParameters:\n  nPaletteIndex (ECX): Index into palette/transform tables (0-6 valid)\n  pdwPaletteResult (EDX): Output pointer to store palette lookup result\n\nReturns:\n  int: Transform mode value from g_pOutputBufferTable structure\n       Returns 0 for invalid indices (>6 or index 5)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_awData_6f899466: DWORD array containing palette lookup values\n  g_pOutputBufferTable (0x6f89bf28): Pointer to output buffer configuration structure\n\nCalled By:\n  FillOrTransformRect - uses return value to select fill/transform algorithm",
