      "comment": "Draws a CEL animation frame to the screen buffer with clipping and transparency.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data from cache; return 0 if failed\n2. Get CEL file properties: table index, mode value, and height\n3. Perform Y-axis clipping check against tile projection offset\n4. Perform X-axis clipping check against buffer height\n5. Select draw table value based on dwDrawMode (0-6, with 7 as special case)\n6. Apply transparency table if dwTransparency byte is not 0xFF\n7. Call D2CMP_DecodeAndDrawCelFrame to render the frame\n\nParameters:\n  ppCelFile (CelFile**) - Pointer to CEL file pointer (ECX)\n  nPosY (int) - Y position for drawing, IMPLICIT in EDX\n  nPosX (int) - X position for drawing\n  dwTransparency (uint) - Transparency byte (0xFF = opaque, other = lookup index >> 3)\n  dwDrawMode (uint) - Draw mode selector (0-7): selects draw table offset\n  dwDrawFlags (uint) - Flags passed to D2CMP_DecodeAndDrawCelFrame\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Frame drawn successfully\n  0 - Frame not drawn (load failed or clipped out of bounds)\n\nDraw Mode Table Offsets:\n  0 -> +0x08, 1 -> +0x04, 2 -> +0x00, 3 -> +0x104\n  4 -> +0x108, 5 -> default (0), 6 -> +0x10c, 7 -> +0x118 (transparency)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early with 0 if LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData fails\n- Clipping uses both tile projection offset and buffer height globals\n- Mode 7 overrides transparency table selection\n\nPhantom Variables:\n- local_4: Stack temporary at [ESP+0x18] used to preserve nPosY (EDX) during function calls",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
