      "name": "DrawCelFrameClipped",
      "signature": "void DrawCelFrameClipped(int * pCelData, int nXPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws a cel (sprite) frame with coordinate bounds validation and clipping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load or retrieve cel frame data for the specified cel data pointer\n2. If frame data is valid, extract cel file info from the pointer\n3. Get cel table index, mode value (offset), and height from cel info\n4. Calculate clipped Y coordinate: (nXPos - celModeValue) + celHeight\n5. Validate Y bounds: clippedY < tile project offset AND combined offset >= 0\n6. Get additional field value and validate X bounds against buffer height\n7. Check for output buffer override via FUN_6f8917e0 palette lookup\n8. Call BlitScaledCmpFrameClipped to perform the actual rendering\n\nParameters:\n    pCelData (ECX): Pointer to cel data structure containing sprite frame info\n    nXPos (EDX): X position offset for rendering the cel frame\n    nYPos (Stack): Y position offset for rendering the cel frame\n\nReturns:\n    void - Renders directly to the frame buffer if all bounds checks pass\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Early exit if LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData returns 0 (invalid frame)\n    - Early exit if calculated Y position exceeds tile project offset\n    - Early exit if combined X/Y offset is negative (off-screen)\n    - Early exit if X position exceeds buffer height bounds\n    - Palette index defaults to 0, overridden by output buffer table if available",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0549f81ee693cd7aaf65fce4f25e12777d4c609fc4c3a53601970ea3d0b726f8",
