      "name": "CheckBitfieldSlotAvailable",
      "signature": "bool CheckBitfieldSlotAvailable(uint * pdwBitfield, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if a bit position in a 32-bit DWORD array is available (clear) and all subsequent DWORDs are also clear.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Calculate target DWORD index by dividing bit index by 32 (0x20)\n2. Calculate bit position within DWORD using modulo operation\n3. Create bit mask using left shift and bitwise NOT to test target bit\n4. Test if target bit is set - if so, position is unavailable, return false\n5. Calculate starting array index (DWORD index + 1) for subsequent checks\n6. If starting index is less than 3, iterate through remaining array elements\n7. Check each DWORD from starting index to index 2 (3 total DWORDs maximum)\n8. If any DWORD contains non-zero value, position is unavailable, return false\n9. If all checks pass, position is available, return true\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBitfield: Pointer to DWORD array used as bitfield (minimum 3 DWORDs, 12 bytes)\n- nBitIndex: Zero-based bit position to check (0-95 for 3 DWORD array)\n\nReturns:\n- true (1): Bit position is clear and all subsequent DWORDs are zero\n- false (0): Bit position is set OR subsequent DWORDs contain non-zero values\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If bit index results in DWORD index 2 or higher, no subsequent DWORD checking needed\n- Function assumes array has at least 3 DWORDs (indices 0, 1, 2)\n- Uses 32-bit arithmetic for bit calculations (0x20 = 32, 0x1f = 31)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per DWORD for index calculation\n- 0x1f (31): Maximum bit position within DWORD (bit mask)\n- 0x1fU (31): Unsigned constant for bit position calculation\n- 3: Maximum array index checked (indices 0, 1, 2)\n- 4: Byte increment for DWORD pointer arithmetic",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:f2ac89765b2a6fcb5aa091f69d5752b26dbdee0836982dd75a34260d01ba9650",
