      "name": "ParseStringToExtendedFloat",
      "signature": "void ParseStringToExtendedFloat(void * this, uint * param_1, byte * param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Parses string input to ExtendedFloat format and converts to standard uint output\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local ExtendedFloat structure on stack\n2. Call string parser with context, extended float buffer, string input, and zero parameters\n3. Convert ExtendedFloat result to standard uint format using predefined configuration\n4. Return to caller with converted output in buffer\n\nParameters:\n  this             - Context object for string parsing operations  \n  pdwOutputBuffer  - Pointer to uint buffer receiving converted numeric result\n  pbInputString    - Pointer to null-terminated string containing numeric value to parse\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, output written directly to pdwOutputBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  String parsing handles multiple formats including scientific notation\n  Extended float provides high precision intermediate representation\n  Conversion uses hardcoded configuration for consistent output format\n\nStructure Layout:\n  ExtendedFloat (12 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field Name      Type     Description\n    +0x00   2     wMantissaLow    ushort   Lower mantissa bits  \n    +0x02   2     wMantissaHigh   ushort   Upper mantissa bits\n    +0x04   4     dwExponent      uint     Exponent component\n    +0x08   4     dwFlags         uint     Sign and format flags",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
