      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeLocale",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitializeLocale(void * this, char * param_1, undefined2 * param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes a locale configuration from a locale string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Ensure locale handler is initialized (0x0041374c):\n     - If not initialized, call InitializeLocaleHandler() \n     - If init fails, set fallback handler to default handler (0x409be1)\n  2. Validate input locale string (param_1):\n     - If NULL or empty, branch to error handling\n  3. Parse locale components from input string:\n     - Copy primary locale component to buffer (0x41373c), max 0x40 (64) bytes\n     - Copy secondary locale component to buffer (0x413740), max 0x40 (64) bytes\n  4. Validate parsed components and select appropriate handler:\n     - If both components present and valid: call GetPrimaryHandler()\n     - If only primary present and valid: call GetDefaultHandler()\n     - If only secondary present: call GetSecondaryHandler()\n     - If none present: call GetErrorHandler()\n  5. If handler found, check for code page data (0x0041372c):\n     - Query code page via IsValidCodePage()\n     - Query locale via IsValidLocale()\n     - If valid, populate output structures:\n       - If pResultCode (param_2) provided: store result code\n       - If bStoreResult (param_3) provided: call StoreLocaleData()\n     - Call FinalizeLocaleConfiguration()\n\nParameters:\n  ECX (this): Pointer to locale manager object\n  param_1 (pLocaleString): Input locale string (e.g., \"en-US\", \"fr-FR\")\n  param_2 (pResultCode): Output buffer for result codes (2 bytes), may be NULL\n  param_3 (bStoreResult): Flag to store result (0x4, 0x5 indicate store level)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 on success (valid locale configured)\n  EAX = 0 on failure (invalid locale, no handler found, or validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty input string \u2192 calls GetErrorHandler\n  - NULL input pointer \u2192 calls GetErrorHandler\n  - Code page lookup fails \u2192 returns 0\n  - Locale validation fails \u2192 returns 0",
