      "name": "GetLocaleInfoByType",
      "signature": "int GetLocaleInfoByType(int nInfoType, LCID dwLocaleId, LCTYPE dwLocaleType, char * szOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves locale-specific information by type, returning either a string or numeric value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check nInfoType to determine retrieval mode (STRING_MODE=1 or NUMERIC_MODE=0)\n2. For NUMERIC_MODE (nInfoType=0):\n   a. Call GetLocaleInfoWideToBuffer to get wide string into global buffer\n   b. Initialize output byte to zero\n   c. Loop through wide characters, checking if digit via GetCharacterProperties\n   d. Accumulate decimal value: result = result * 10 + (char - '0')\n3. For STRING_MODE (nInfoType=1):\n   a. First try 128-byte stack buffer via GetLocaleInfoAnsiToBuffer\n   b. If ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER (0x7a), query required size and malloc\n   c. Call GetLocaleInfoAnsiToBuffer with allocated buffer\n   d. Allocate output buffer via malloc and copy result with strncpy\n   e. Free source buffer if dynamically allocated\n4. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n- nInfoType: Retrieval mode (0=numeric value, 1=string allocation)\n- dwLocaleId: Windows LCID locale identifier\n- dwLocaleType: LCTYPE constant specifying which locale info to retrieve\n- szOutput: For NUMERIC_MODE, pointer to byte receiving parsed value\n            For STRING_MODE, pointer to char* receiving allocated string\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success (szOutput populated with result)\n- -1: Failure (GetLocaleInfo failed, malloc failed, or invalid nInfoType)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nInfoType other than 0 or 1 returns -1 immediately\n- Large strings exceeding 128 bytes trigger dynamic allocation\n- Caller responsible for freeing returned string in STRING_MODE\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80 (128): Stack buffer size for ANSI string\n- 0x7a (122): ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER Windows error code\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0' for digit conversion\n- 0x0a (10): Decimal base multiplier\n- 4: Wide character buffer size (4 WCHARs)",
