      "name": "Int64ToCharUnsigned",
      "signature": "char * Int64ToCharUnsigned(uint dwValueLo, uint dwValueHi, char * szOutput, uint dwRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts an unsigned 64-bit integer to a null-terminated string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls Int64ToCharInternal with nIsSigned=0 (unsigned mode)\n2. Returns the output buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n- dwValueLo (uint): Low 32 bits of 64-bit value\n- dwValueHi (uint): High 32 bits of 64-bit value\n- szOutput (char*): Output buffer for string result\n- dwRadix (uint): Numeric base for conversion (e.g., 10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\n\nReturns:\n- szOutput pointer (for chaining)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Int64ToCharInternal: Core conversion with signed/unsigned flag",
