      "name": "GetLocaleInfoAnsiToBuffer",
      "signature": "int GetLocaleInfoAnsiToBuffer(dword lcid, dword lcType, dword pszBuffer, int nBufferSize, dword dwCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves locale information and converts result to ANSI if needed\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if Unicode/ANSI code page support has been cached in g_dwLocaleInfoCodePageCache (0=uncached, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n  2. If not cached, probe both GetLocaleInfoW (0x40d110) and GetLocaleInfoA (0x40d124) with test parameters\n  3. Store support type in cache: 1 for Unicode capable, 2 for ANSI only\n  4. If Unicode capable (cache=1), query required buffer size from GetLocaleInfoW, allocate temp buffer on stack, retrieve Unicode result, convert to ANSI via WideCharToMultiByte (0x40d164) with code page parameter\n  5. If ANSI only (cache=2), call GetLocaleInfoA directly with parameters\n  6. Return character count (including null terminator) or 0 on error\n\nParameters:\n  lcid: Locale identifier for GetLocaleInfo APIs\n  lcType: Locale information type constant (e.g., 0x1 for LOCALE_IDEFAULTCODEPAGE)\n  pszBuffer: Output buffer pointer for ANSI result (NULL = size query only)\n  cchBuffer: Size of output buffer in characters (0 = size query)\n  dwCodePage: Code page for Unicode to ANSI conversion (0 = use g_dwDefaultCodePage)\n\nReturns:\n  Positive: Number of characters in result including null terminator\n  Zero: GetLocaleInfo failed or no API available\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If cchBuffer is 0 and pszBuffer is non-NULL, returns required buffer size\n  - If dwCodePage is 0, substitutes g_dwDefaultCodePage instead\n  - ProbeStack (0x405820) verifies stack space before allocating temporary Unicode buffer\n  - Set-up code handles SEH (Structured Exception Handling) for stack probe safety\n  - WideCharToMultiByte flags: 0x220 (error on invalid chars + best fit)",
