      "name": "InitializeGammaCorrection",
      "signature": "void InitializeGammaCorrection(int nUnknownParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes gamma correction lookup tables for palette color transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load gamma value from g_nGammaValue as floating-point\n  2. Store ECX parameter to g_nGammaParam\n  3. Allocate 0x100 (256) byte buffer on stack\n  4. Call GenerateGammaTable with:\n     - nGammaValue: from FPU stack\n     - pOutTable: stack buffer (EDX)\n     - dPercentLinear: 1.0 (0x3FF00000)\n     - nEntrySize: 0x100 (256)\n     - nEntryCount: 0xFF (255)\n  5. Loop 0x400 (1024) iterations copying from g_aGammaLookupTable\n     to palette RGB entries at g_dwScreenHeight area\n  6. Set g_dwPaletteUpdateNeeded = 1 to trigger palette refresh\n  7. Cleanup stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  nUnknownParam (ECX) - Stored to g_nGammaParam, purpose unclear\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function body is fragmented in Ghidra (only FILD instruction visible)\n  - Full function spans 0x6f8e2340-0x6f8e23bf (0x80 bytes)\n\nNOTE: Function boundaries broken - manual repair needed in Ghidra.\n      Use \"Create Function\" at 0x6f8e2340 after disassembling 0x6f8e2346-0x6f8e23bf.",
