      "name": "FillRectangleWithPattern",
      "signature": "void FillRectangleWithPattern(tagRECT * pRect, byte fillByte)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Fills a rectangular region with a repeating byte pattern using optimized 32-bit memory writes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input rectangle bounds: top <= bottom, left <= right\n2. Call GetReturnAddress() and CleanupAndAbort() if validation fails\n3. Load boundary constants from globals: DAT_6f8d01c8 (max Y), DAT_6f8d01d8 (max X)\n4. Validate rectangle is within bounds, clamp coordinates to valid ranges\n5. If left < 0, set to 0; if right >= maxY, set to maxY-1\n6. If top < 0, set to 0; if bottom >= maxX, set to maxX-1\n7. Calculate width and height as differences\n8. For each row in rectangle (height iterations):\n   - Calculate linear memory offset: base + (top * stride) + left\n   - Fill width bytes with pattern using STOSD (dword) for 4-byte chunks\n   - Fill remaining bytes (width % 4) with STOSB (byte)\n9. Advance base pointer by screen stride to next row\n10. Return after all rows filled\n\nParameters:\n- pRect (ECX): Pointer to tagRECT structure containing left, top, right, bottom bounds\n- fillByte (DL): Single byte value to fill rectangle with (replicated in dword)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Line 0x165, 0x166: Magic error numbers for validation failures, passed to CleanupAndAbort\n- DAT_6f8d01c8: Global containing screen width in pixels (max Y coordinate)\n- DAT_6f8d01d8: Global containing screen height in pixels (max X coordinate)\n- DAT_6f8cf8a8: Global containing base screen buffer address\n- Bounds are inclusive-exclusive: right and bottom are treated as exclusive bounds\n- Rectangle size is (right - left) * (bottom - top) pixels\n- Byte replication: fillByte expanded to 0xBBBBBBBB in EAX for dword writes\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type      Description\n0       4     left            LONG      Left edge coordinate\n4       4     top             LONG      Top edge coordinate\n8       4     right           LONG      Right edge coordinate\n12      4     bottom          LONG      Bottom edge coordinate\nTotal: 16 bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
