      "name": "InitializeGameMemoryBuffers",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameMemoryBuffers(int nConditionFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game memory buffers based on DirectDraw surface creation. Creates a DirectDraw surface with specified capacity and clears memory according to condition flag. If surface creation succeeds with code 0x887601ae, calculates buffer size and clears game memory. Otherwise, logs DirectDraw error via MapDirectDrawErrorToString.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local DirectDraw capabilities structure (0x64 bytes)\n2. Check if global DirectDraw interface pointer is valid\n3. Call DirectDraw CreateSurface with capabilities and 0x400 flag\n4. Check if surface creation returned valid result\n5. Compare result code against success code 0x887601ae\n6. If success: Calculate memory size based on condition flag (subtract 0x2f if flag set)\n7. Multiply by multiplier from DAT_6f8d01c8\n8. Clear calculated bytes from DAT_6f8cf8a8 using REP STOSD/STOSB\n9. If error: Call MapDirectDrawErrorToString to log DirectDraw error\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\n- nConditionFlag (ECX): Condition affecting buffer size calculation (0=use base size, non-0=subtract 0x2f from count)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Success code 0x887601ae indicates successful DirectDraw surface creation\n- Uses mixed REP instructions: STOSD for 4-byte chunks, STOSB for remaining bytes\n- Global DAT_6f8d01c8 is a multiplier for final byte count calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
