      "name": "DrawPointRectangleWithPattern",
      "signature": "void DrawPointRectangleWithPattern(int * pCoordinate, char nThickness, byte nPattern)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draw a rectangle outline at a point with specified thickness and pattern fill.\n\nThis function expands a point coordinate in all directions by a thickness value,\ncreates a rectangle boundary, and fills it with a specified pattern. The thickness\nis decremented by 1 before expansion, so a thickness of 1 produces no expansion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if thickness parameter is zero; if so, return without drawing\n2. Decrement thickness value to get expansion amount\n3. Load X and Y coordinates from pointer parameter\n4. Expand rectangle bounds in all directions by expansion amount\n5. Call SetRect to define rectangle boundaries\n6. Call FillRectangleWithPattern to fill with specified pattern\n7. Return\n\nParameters:\npCoordinate (int*): Pointer to coordinate array where [0]=X, [1]=Y center point\nnThickness (char): Border thickness/expansion value (1=point only, 2=expand by 1, etc)\nnPattern (byte): Fill pattern byte for rectangle interior\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thickness of 0 causes early exit with no drawing\n- Thickness of 1 produces a 1-pixel rectangle at the coordinate point\n- Higher thickness values produce larger rectangles expanding outward from center",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:42dde519139f8bfa187b5fae5d5b8f4ee215833f6d18c2170b2cc314b173469a",
