      "name": "DrawLine",
      "signature": "void DrawLine(int x0, int y0, int x1, int y1, uchar pixelValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a line using Bresenham's line algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load screen width from global DAT_6f8d01c8\n2. Calculate delta X and delta Y from endpoint coordinates\n3. Determine X direction (1 if increasing, -1 if decreasing)\n4. Determine Y direction (1 if increasing, -1 if decreasing)\n5. Validate start pixel coordinates against screen bounds\n6. If start pixel is valid, draw it with the specified pixel value\n7. Determine major axis (compare absolute deltas) to choose iteration strategy\n8. If Y is major axis: iterate over Y, accumulate X error, increment X when error exceeds Y delta\n9. If X is major axis: iterate over X, accumulate Y error, increment Y when error exceeds X delta\n10. For each pixel, validate bounds and write pixel value if in bounds\n11. Continue until all pixels along the line are processed\n\nParameters:\n- x0: Starting X coordinate (column)\n- y0: Starting Y coordinate (row)\n- x1: Ending X coordinate (column)\n- y1: Ending Y coordinate (row)\n- pixelValue: 8-bit value to write for each pixel\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies screen buffer in place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Out-of-bounds pixels are skipped without error\n- Diagonal lines use Y-major axis by default\n- Single-pixel lines draw only the start pixel",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
