      "name": "RenderCharacterToGrid",
      "signature": "uint RenderCharacterToGrid(void * this, uint gridX, char charCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders a character glyph to a 16x8 pixel grid at the specified coordinate.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate gridCoord is in range [0, 0x280)\n2. If gridCoord < 0, return color from DAT_6f8cf500[charCode]\n3. If charCode < 0x20 or >= 0x7F, return default color from DAT_6f8cf500\n4. Calculate character offset: (charCode - 0x20) * 4 from DAT_6f8cf380\n5. Retrieve character bitmap data from table at calculated offset + DAT_6f8d01f4\n6. Calculate pixel grid address: gridStride * gridX + DAT_6f8cf8a8 + gridCoord\n7. Loop 16 times (once per row):\n   a. Read 8 bytes from character bitmap (one row of 8 pixels)\n   b. For each non-zero byte: write 0xFF to pixel grid (lit pixel)\n   c. Move to next row: pPixelGrid += gridStride, pCharBitmap += 8\n8. Return character color attribute from DAT_6f8cf500[charCode - 0x20]\n\nParameters:\n  gridCoord (ECX): Grid coordinate in range [0, 0x280); negative values use alternate lookup\n  charCode (AL): ASCII character code to render; valid range [0x20, 0x7E]\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: Color/attribute value for the character from DAT_6f8cf500 table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - gridCoord >= 0x280: Returns 0 (out of bounds)\n  - gridCoord < 0: Returns color from DAT_6f8cf500[charCode] without rendering\n  - charCode < 0x20 or >= 0x7F: Returns default color, no rendering\n\nData Structures:\n  DAT_6f8cf380: Character bitmap offset table (256 entries, 4 bytes each)\n  DAT_6f8cf500: Character color/attribute table (256 entries, 4 bytes each)\n  DAT_6f8cf8a8: Base address of pixel grid buffer\n  DAT_6f8d01c8: Grid stride/width in bytes per row\n  DAT_6f8d01f4: Character bitmap data base address offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
