      "name": "RenderEntityWithCel",
      "signature": "void RenderEntityWithCel(int pEntity, int yCoord)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders an entity (unit/monster) using cel graphics animation at specified screen coordinates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize entity with animation slots\n2. Calculate animation coordinates and frame index\n3. If calculation succeeds, retrieve animation frame data\n4. Draw cel graphic at computed screen position with offsets\n5. Cleanup and return\n\nParameters:\npEntity (ECX): Pointer to entity structure containing animation/mode data\nyCoord (EDX): Y-coordinate for rendering on screen\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout (Entity @ offset +0x3c):\nAnimation mode/state field accessed at offset +0x3c\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function exits early (init_entity_failed) if entity initialization fails\n- Function exits early (coords_calculation_failed) if coordinate calculation fails\n- Uses uninitialized local variables for offset/coordinate calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
