      "name": "MapDirectDrawErrorToString",
      "signature": "void MapDirectDrawErrorToString(void * this, int hResult, undefined4 param_FormatArg)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Maps a DirectDraw HRESULT error code to a human-readable error message string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for early return codes (0x887601ae, 0x887601c2) that immediately exit\n2. Perform binary search through nested comparisons to narrow down the error code range\n3. Use indexed table lookups with bounds checking for common error code groups:\n   - Table 1: Error codes in range [-0x7789ffec, -0x7789ffec+0x50)\n   - Table 2: Error codes in range [-0x7789ff88, -0x7789ff88+0x64)\n   - Table 3: Error codes in range [-0x7789ff1f, -0x7789ff1f+0xd2)\n   - Table 4: Error codes in range [-0x7789fe3e, -0x7789fe3e+0x7e)\n   - Table 5: Error codes in range [-0x7789fdbe, -0x7789fdbe+0x2a)\n4. Handle special case codes: 0x8007000e (OUT_OF_MEMORY), 0x80004001 (UNSUPPORTED), \n   0x80004005 (GENERIC), 0x800401f0 (NOT_INITIALIZED), 0x80070057 (INVALID_PARAMS), \n   0x88760005 (ALREADY_INITIALIZED)\n5. For unknown codes, return default error message \"<unknown>\"\n6. For success code (0x0), return \"DD_OK\"\n7. Call ValidateAndInitializeParameter to format and log the error string with context\n\nParameters:\n  hResult (ECX): DirectDraw HRESULT error code to map\n  param_FormatArg (Stack[0x4]): Additional parameter passed to logging function\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value, function performs side effects through ValidateAndInitializeParameter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Code 0x887601ae and 0x887601c2 cause immediate return without any action\n  - Code 0x0 maps to success string \"DD_OK\"\n  - Codes outside all known ranges map to default \"<unknown>\" message\n  - All other codes map to DirectDraw-specific error strings\n  - Function uses table-driven dispatch with offset calculation for performance",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
