      "name": "ValidateAndCleanupGraphicsSurfaces",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndCleanupGraphicsSurfaces(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes DirectDraw surfaces for graphics rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if secondary surface is enabled (DAT_6f8d0234)\n2. If enabled and valid secondary surface exists, perform BltFast from secondary to primary\n3. If BltFast fails, log error and return 0\n4. If not enabled but valid primary surface exists, call primary surface method at offset 0x2c\n5. Check if palette update is pending (DAT_6f8d0240)\n6. If pending and valid palette surface exists, call SetEntries method at offset 0x18\n7. If SetEntries fails, log error and return 0\n8. Return 1 (success) if all operations completed without error\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global DirectDraw surface pointers (DAT_6f8d0218, DAT_6f8d0220, DAT_6f8d021c, DAT_6f8d0230, DAT_6f8d0240)\n\nReturns:\nuint - 1 if successful, 0 if BltFast or SetEntries operations failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skips operations if secondary surface pointer is NULL\n- Handles case where secondary and primary surfaces are the same\n- Clears pending palette flag (DAT_6f8d0240) after palette update\n- Error strings: \"BltFast_failed\" at 0x6f8ccc04, \"SetEntries_failed\" at 0x6f8ccbf0",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
