      "name": "DrawScaledCmpFrameClipped",
      "signature": "void DrawScaledCmpFrameClipped(int * pnCelFile, int nYPos, int nXPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws a scaled CMP frame to the screen with clipping against surface boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data for the specified CelFile\n2. If frame data loaded successfully, extract CelFileInfo pointer\n3. Get table index, mode value, and height from CelFile metadata\n4. Calculate adjusted Y position: (nYPos - modeValue) + height\n5. Bounds check: Verify adjusted Y is within surface width\n6. Bounds check: Verify combined coordinates are non-negative\n7. Get DWORD field for X offset calculation\n8. Bounds check: Verify X position is non-negative\n9. Bounds check: Verify X offset within display height\n10. Get video player context to determine palette index\n11. If video context exists, use current buffer for palette; otherwise use 0\n12. Call BlitScaledCmpFrameClipped with all calculated parameters\n\nParameters:\npnCelFile (ECX) - Pointer to CelFile structure handle\nnYPos (EDX) - Y position for rendering\nnXPos (Stack) - X position for rendering\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData fails (returns 0)\n- Early exit if adjusted Y >= surface width\n- Early exit if combined coordinate check fails (< 0)\n- Early exit if X position < 0\n- Early exit if X offset >= display height\n- Palette index defaults to 0 if no video player context",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
