      "comment": "Fills or blits a video region with color at a specific intensity level.\\n\\nConverts an 8-bit intensity value (0-255) into a discrete intensity level (0-5) and calls FillOrBlitVideoRegion with the corresponding level. This function maps intensity ranges as follows:\\n- intensity > 0xBF (192): Level 5 (highest intensity)\\n- 0x80 (128) < intensity <= 0xBF: Level 2 (mid-high intensity)\\n- 0x40 (64) < intensity <= 0x7F: Level 1 (mid-low intensity)\\n- 0 < intensity <= 0x40: Level 0 (lowest intensity)\\n- intensity = 0: No fill operation\\n\\nParameters:\\n- left: Left edge X coordinate of the region\\n- top: Top edge Y coordinate of the region\\n- width: Width of the region in pixels\\n- height: Height of the region in pixels\\n- color: Color index or palette value to use for filling\\n- intensity: Intensity value (0-255) determining fill level\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Modifies the video buffer directly",
