      "name": "ProcessFormattedStringWithCallback",
      "signature": "void ProcessFormattedStringWithCallback(void * pDataBuffer, int nInitialOffset, LPCSTR pFormatString, va_list vaArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes a formatted string by invoking a callback for each character, with special handling for newlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format input string using wvsprintfA with provided format and variadic arguments into 512-byte buffer\n2. Initialize character counter to 0 and current buffer position to input pointer\n3. If formatted string has at least 1 character (length > 0), enter processing loop:\n   a. Load current character from formatted buffer at current index\n   b. Invoke callback function at 0x6f8c9340 with current buffer position and offset parameter\n   c. Advance buffer position by returned offset value\n   d. Check if current character is newline (0x0a)\n   e. If newline detected, reset buffer position to original input pointer and increment offset by 0xc\n   f. Increment character counter and continue until all characters processed\n4. Clean up stack and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pDataBuffer (ECX): Pointer to data structure or buffer to be processed\n- nInitialOffset (EDX): Initial offset parameter passed to callback function (incremented by 0xc on newline)\n- pFormatString: Pointer to format string for wvsprintfA\n- vaArgs: Variadic arguments for string formatting\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty strings (length <= 0): Function skips callback loop entirely\n- Newline handling: Resets buffer pointer and increments offset by 0xc (0x0c = 12 bytes), suggesting 3-element structure\n- Magic number 0xc: Likely size of single data element in target structure",
