      "name": "ShutdownModuleResources",
      "signature": "int ShutdownModuleResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Cleanup and shutdown all module resources.\n\nEnsures proper cleanup of all active module resources by checking and\nreleasing each critical resource in a specific order. This function is\ncalled during module shutdown to prevent resource leaks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if module is initialized (global at 0x6f8d0200)\n   - If not initialized, call FUN_6f8c8b40 to initialize first\n2. Release first resource (pointer at 0x6f8d0230)\n   - If non-NULL, call virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n3. Release second resource (pointer at 0x6f8d0214)\n   - If non-NULL, call virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n4. Release third resource (pointer at 0x6f8d0210)\n   - If non-NULL, call virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n5. Release fourth resource (pointer at 0x6f8d023c)\n   - If non-NULL, call virtual destructor at 0x6f8cb174\n   - Then call additional cleanup function 0x6f8c5f3a with size 0x122\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n6. Release fifth resource (pointer at 0x6f8d01f4)\n   - If non-NULL, call cleanup function 0x6f8c5f3a with size 0x5d\n   - Clear the pointer to NULL\n7. Clear module initialization flag (set global at 0x6f8d0200 to 0)\n8. Return 1 (success status)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success (shutdown completed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if module not initialized: skips to cleanup_done\n- Each resource check skips cleanup if pointer is NULL\n- Global at 0x6f8cfdc4 is cleared during second resource cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
