      "name": "InitializeDirectDrawAndCriticalSection",
      "signature": "int InitializeDirectDrawAndCriticalSection(uint screenWidth, uint screenHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize DirectDraw graphics interface and critical section for thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store screen dimensions in global variables (DAT_6f8d01d0, DAT_6f8d01dc)\n2. Initialize font bitmap resources via InitializeFontBitmap()\n3. Check if bit masks are available by testing gdwBitMasks_exref & DAT_6f8cfcb0\n4. Set bit masks pointer to DAT_6f8cfcb4 if available, otherwise use NULL\n5. Create DirectDraw object via DirectDrawCreate() with bit masks pointer\n6. If DirectDraw creation fails (return value is non-zero), log error and return 0\n7. Register cleanup handler via atexit() to call cleanup at LAB_6f8c8e70\n8. Set initialization flag DAT_6f8d0200 to 1\n9. Allocate critical section structure (0xF3 bytes) via AllocateMemoryWithTracking()\n10. Initialize critical section for thread-safe graphics operations\n11. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n  screenWidth (ECX) - Screen width or rendering parameter\n  screenHeight (EDX) - Screen height or rendering parameter\n\nReturns:\n  1 on successful initialization\n  0 if DirectDraw creation fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - DirectDraw failure causes immediate error return (value 0)\n  - Bit masks selection depends on gdwBitMasks_exref & DAT_6f8cfcb0 test result\n  - Critical section allocated with 0xF3 bytes for synchronization primitive\n  - atexit() handler ensures cleanup on program exit",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
