      "name": "DisplaySecurityErrorDialog",
      "signature": "void DisplaySecurityErrorDialog(int errorType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Security error handler that displays a message box with buffer overrun or security failure information. Checks for custom exception handler first, then builds an error dialog with module name, error type, and description. Exits with code 3 after user interaction.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize stack canary and save exception handler address\\n2. Check if custom exception handler is installed (DAT_6f8cf2a8)\\n3. If custom handler exists, call it with error type and exit with code 3\\n4. Otherwise, determine error message based on error type (1=buffer overrun, other=security failure)\\n5. Retrieve module filename via GetModuleFileNameA, use default if fails\\n6. Calculate total message length (module name + header + description)\\n7. If length exceeds 60 chars, truncate module name with ellipsis\\n8. Assemble error message by concatenating: error_type + separator + program_name + module_name + separator + error_description\\n9. Display message box with MB_ICONERROR | MB_TOPMOST flags (0x12010)\\n10. Exit process with code 3\\n\\nParameters:\\n  errorType [int] - Error type: 1 for buffer overrun, other values for unknown security failure\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - Never returns; function calls exit(3) to terminate process\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - If GetModuleFileNameA fails, displays '<program_name_unknown>' as fallback\\n  - If assembled message exceeds 60 character limit, truncates module name to fit and appends '...'\\n  - Stack canary (stackCanary) protects against buffer overflow attacks\\n  - Custom handler at DAT_6f8cf2a8 can intercept error before dialog is shown\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n  moduleNameBuffer[65 * 4 bytes] - 260-byte buffer for module path\\n  Message buffer constructed on-stack in local_1c area for dialog display",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
