      "name": "InitializeNetworkCachePoolAndExecuteCallback",
      "signature": "void InitializeNetworkCachePoolAndExecuteCallback(void * pCacheObject, int callbackType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a network cache pool and executes an associated callback function with a calculated offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save callee-preserved registers ESI and EDI\n2. Move ECX (pCacheObject) to ESI, EDX (callbackType) to EDI\n3. Call InitializeNetworkCachePool with pCacheObject, flag=1, and 0\n4. If initialization fails (EAX == 0), jump to cleanup\n5. Based on callbackType value (1 or 2):\n   - Type 1: Calculate offset = (GlobalCount >> 2)\n   - Type 2: Calculate offset = -(GlobalCount >> 2)\n   - Other: Use offset as-is from stack parameter\n6. Fetch callback function pointer from DAT_6f8d01dc+0xc\n7. Call callback with pCacheObject in ECX and calculated offset in EDX\n8. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pCacheObject (ECX): Pointer to cache pool object to initialize\n  callbackType (EDX): Callback type selector (1=positive, 2=negative, other=no adjustment)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If InitializeNetworkCachePool fails, callback is not executed\n  - GlobalCount at 0x6f8d01c8 is divided by 4 with arithmetic right shift\n  - Negative offset calculation uses NEG instruction for type 2",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6abcc731a6dfa7e0b993f3b20da37c0a",
