      "name": "DrawLine",
      "signature": "void DrawLine(int * pStartPos, int * pEndPos, undefined1 pixelColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Draws a line between two points using Bresenham's line algorithm with fixed-point arithmetic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load start point (x0, y0) from pStartPos and end point (x1, y1) from pEndPos\n2. Calculate delta components: deltaX = x1-x0, deltaY = y1-y0\n3. Compute squared distance: distanceSquared = deltaX\u00b2+deltaY\u00b2\n4. Calculate step distance (sqrt approximation) using integer loop until stepDistance\u00b2 \u2265 distanceSquared\n5. Convert deltas to fixed-point by scaling by 0x10000 and dividing by stepDistance\n6. Initialize error accumulators errorX and errorY to 0\n7. Loop through each step from 0 to stepDistance:\n   - Check bounds: if current (x,y) outside valid map bounds, exit early\n   - Accumulate errorX += scaledDeltaX; if overflow, update x and clear fractional part\n   - Accumulate errorY += scaledDeltaY; if overflow, update y and clear fractional part\n8. Plot current pixel at map position using given color, then increment step counter\n9. Continue until all pixels in line segment are plotted or bounds exceeded\n\nParameters:\n  pStartPos: Pointer to int array [startX, startY] - starting coordinates\n  pEndPos: Pointer to int array [endX, endY] - ending coordinates\n  pixelColor: Byte value for pixel color to plot\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Exits early if either endpoint falls outside map bounds (0 to mapWidth-1, 0 to mapHeight-1)\n  - Uses fixed-point arithmetic (0x10000 = 1.0) for subpixel precision during stepping\n  - Fixed-point overflow at \u00b10xFFFF triggers coordinate update with SAR 0x10 to extract integer part\n  - All pixels outside bounds are skipped without drawing",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d5cabd666c729ed6b66a2ccb2a65728c",
