      "name": "DrawRectangle",
      "signature": "void DrawRectangle(tagRECT * pRect, uchar color)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Draws a rectangle outline on the screen using four lines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load rectangle coordinates from structure: left (offset 0x0), top (offset 0x4), right (offset 0x8), bottom (offset 0xc)\n2. Validate horizontal bounds: left must be <= right, else abort with error 0x149\n3. Validate vertical bounds: top must be <= bottom, else abort with error 0x14a\n4. Check if rectangle has non-zero width (right != left) and non-zero height (bottom != top)\n5. If rectangle dimensions are valid, draw four lines connecting the four corners:\n   - Line 1: (top, left) to (bottom, left) - left edge\n   - Line 2: (bottom, left) to (bottom, right) - bottom edge\n   - Line 3: (left, right) to (top, right) - right edge\n   - Line 4: (left, top) to (left, bottom) - top edge\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pRect (tagRECT*): Pointer to rectangle structure with fields left, top, right, bottom in DWORDs\n  color (unsigned char): Color value passed to DrawLine for line rendering\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function returns normally after drawing or validation failure causes abort\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-width rectangles (left == right) skip drawing\n  - Zero-height rectangles (top == bottom) skip drawing\n  - Coordinate validation ensures left <= right and top <= bottom\n  - Invalid coordinates trigger CleanupAndAbort() which terminates process\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name | Type        | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | left       | int/long    | Left edge x-coordinate\n  0x4    | 4    | top        | int/long    | Top edge y-coordinate  \n  0x8    | 4    | right      | int/long    | Right edge x-coordinate\n  0xc    | 4    | bottom     | int/long    | Bottom edge y-coordinate\n  Total size: 16 bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
