      "name": "ValidateAndUpsampleChromaCoordinates",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndUpsampleChromaCoordinates(int xCoord, int yCoord)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates video coordinate bounds and performs chroma data upsampling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate xCoord: must be >= 1 and < (g_VideoWidth - 0x50)\n2. Validate yCoord: must be >= 1 and < (g_VideoHeight - 0x50)\n3. If x validation fails, prepare error code 0x186\n4. If y validation fails, prepare error code 0x187\n5. If both valid, calculate buffer offset and call UpsampleChromaData\n6. If invalid, call GetReturnAddress to get error location and CleanupAndAbort\n\nParameters:\n- xCoord (ECX): X coordinate for chroma data, 1-based index\n- yCoord (EDX): Y coordinate for chroma data, 1-based index\n\nReturns:\n- void, but calls _exit(-1) on validation failure (no return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0x186: X coordinate out of bounds\n- Error code 0x187: Y coordinate out of bounds\n- Both coordinates must be positive and within video dimensions minus 0x50 offset\n- The offset calculation multiplies yCoord by video width before adding xCoord\n- Uses video memory pointer at DAT_6f8cf8a8 as base address",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:7fe7f916c89220ed4f41a858ff890096",
