      "name": "CopyDataBlockAndStorePointer",
      "signature": "void CopyDataBlockAndStorePointer(undefined4 * pSourceData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies a 288-byte data block to a buffer and stores the buffer pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load source data pointer from ECX (parameter in __fastcall convention)\n2. Initialize destination pointer to 0x6f8cf788 (static buffer)\n3. Set copy counter to 0x48 (72 iterations of 4-byte elements = 288 bytes)\n4. Loop: Copy 4-byte blocks from source to destination, incrementing pointers\n5. Store destination buffer pointer at address 0x6f8cf784 for later access\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npSourceData (ECX): Pointer to source data buffer (undefined4 array of 72 elements)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size is fixed at 0x48 * 4 = 288 bytes\n- Destination buffer is at fixed address 0x6f8cf788\n- Pointer to destination is stored at 0x6f8cf784 for external reference\n- Uses REP MOVSD for efficient bulk copy operation\n- Called via data reference from 0x6f8ce98c (indirect/virtual call)\n\nData Layout:\nSource buffer: 72 undefined4 elements = 288 bytes total\nDestination buffer (DAT_6f8cf788): 72 undefined4 elements = 288 bytes total\nPointer storage (DAT_6f8cf784): address of destination buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
